<h4 class="boldbyline">
Re: Cheryl Wehlau's Iron Fist
</h4>

<p>
Tom, I agree. This is fine work by Jeff. As for the distinction between reports and stories, I see it as a spectrum.  One end is pure report.  The other end is pure story.  Jeff's story may not have the elements we'd expect in pure narrative: scenes, dialogue.  But I think something is going on that I don't have a name for.  Impure narrative.  Dirty narrative.  The story of these scumbags abuse is told second and third hand.  And there are enough details to help us imagine how it all went down.  The evidence in the story helps me as a reader fill in the narrative pieces.  So maybe a report can create a movie in our heads.
</p>
